## 4. ATTACK RESULTS — HEADLINE: two falsifying shapes, both reproduced at the FIXED state

### Attack 1 (xs-enummod): two payload enums in ONE module, owners in different modules → **cargo 101 at post** — FALSIFIED

Fixture (my construction, archived at `evidence/attack-fixture-xs-enummod/`):
`Faults.hx` declares BOTH `F1Fault.One` and `F2Fault.Two`; carriers `E1`/`E2`
sit in separate modules `E1.hx`/`E2.hx` (so `exceptionPayloads`, the axis the
fix repairs, does NOT collide). The set site (Compiler.hx:1034-1037) writes
`payloadEnumModules/Names/Owners` keyed by the ENUM module — all three are
last-scanned-wins. The changed site #4 (RustType.hx:148-152) resolves
`payloadModule` correctly per class, but then reads the name and the emission
target from the still-module-keyed maps:

```
use crate::xsxm::e2::F1Fault;   <-- wrong: F1Fault is emitted in xsxm::e1
error[E0432]: unresolved import `crate::xsxm::e2::F1Fault`  (×2, cargo 101)
```

`Compiling`=1, fresh target dir (`evidence/attack.cargo.err`). So "emission
location is genuinely a module property" (REPORT §2, sites #13-20, #26-27) is
WRONG for this shape: the emission itself landed per-owner correctly, but the
module-keyed target map fed the import the sibling's module. The inventory's
"safe" judgements for sites #13/#14/#15-19/#22/#26/#27/#33-35 are all
invalidated by this shape; §7.2's "untested axis" is actually a broken axis.
The fix's changed sites do NOT rescue it — site #4 itself emits the bad value.

### Attack 2 (xs-sibmod): message-only exception + payload exception in ONE module → cargo 101, pre-existing (not a fix regression) — refutes "no known shape reaches it"

Fixture archived at `evidence/attack-fixture-xs-sibmod/`. `RustType.hx` branch 1
gates on `state.messageOnlyExceptions.exists(cls.module)` — a module-keyed
exists() the inventory never examined (it counted only `.get(`). With
`MsgOnly` (String ctor) and `WithPayload` (payload) in one module `Sib.hx`,
the generated crate mixes both representations (`pub struct WithPayload` AND
`F1Fault::WithPayloadFault(Box<WithPayload>)`) and fails: E0308 + E0277,
cargo 101, `Compiling`=1 (`evidence/attack2.cargo.err`). Generated tree is
byte-identical pre vs post the fix (only Cargo.lock differs) → pre-existing
residual, same family as the fixer's documented #5/#7/#25 fall-through, but
the fixer's "no known shape reaches it" is now false: here is a reachable
shape.

